  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is\n\n\\[\\dfrac{2+4+6}{1+3+5} - \\dfrac{1+3+5}{2+4+6}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{36}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{12}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{147}{60}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{43}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First evaluate the sums in the numerators and denominators: \\(2+4+6=12\\) and \\(1+3+5=9\\). The expression becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac{9}{12}\n=\\frac43-\\frac34\n=\\frac{16}{12}-\\frac9{12}\n=\\boxed{\\frac7{12}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
